#!/usr/local/bin/dyalogscript
⍝ csubary.apls -- Dyalog APL, the array form (2026).
⍝ The whole kernel is one expression: the input matrix plus the outer sum
⍝ of the row and column index vectors, (⍳ny)∘.+⍳nx. Built each call, like
⍝ numpy "arrays" and J's csubraw.ijs. Compare csubraw.apls (loops). The
⍝ input is offset by 0.5 so it stays floating point (see csubraw.apls).
⍝ Run as
⍝    dyalogscript csubary.apls 1000 2000 10
⎕IO←0
csub←{in nx ny←⍵ ⋄ in+(⍳ny)∘.+⍳nx}
args←2⎕NQ#'GetCommandLineArgs'
(nrpt nx ny)←⍎¨¯3↑(1↓args),(0⌈4-≢args)↑'1000' '2000' '10'
in←0.5+(nx+ny)-(⍳ny)∘.+⍳nx
⎕←'Arrays ',(⍕nx),' by ',(⍕ny),' count ',⍕nrpt
:For r :In ⍳nrpt
    out←csub in nx ny
:EndFor
:If ∨/,out≠in+(⍳ny)∘.+⍳nx
    ⎕←'Error: result does not match'
:EndIf
